= Experimental Setup

Ten deterministic runs start at 20 C and use a 50 C target, a 0.2 s sampling interval, and a 60 s limit. Settling time is the first time after which the absolute error remains below 1 C. The reported steady-state error is the absolute final error. All conditions and outputs are synthetic and were selected only to exercise the software workflow.

